  "entries": [
    {
      "id": "polar-regions-basal-melt-ocean",
      "topicId": "polar-regions",
      "sourceOrder": 71,
      "status": "READY_FOR_SAME_READER_FINAL",
      "beforeHash": "45f60225f217e7371b9875a18d3432a6d9e8183fe8ccf10b36b4cc8c0cc3c175",
      "literalGroups": [
        {
          "group": "prompt_ordered_answers_key",
          "literal": {
            "prompt": "В первых нескольких сотнях километров плавучей части шельфа Эймери теряется более половины поступающего льда. Какой процесс вызывает эту потерю?",
            "answers": [
              "базальное таяние",
              "подпирающее действие шельфа",
              "неустойчивость морского ледникового щита",
              "откалывание айсбергов"
            ],
            "correctIndex": 0
          },
          "literalSHA256": "e4fecf73109d75c18595d88b0a18a19fe16c26bee397dae5423a09833e949c39",
          "primaryGround": "AAP describes the Amery Ice Shelf and states that more than 50% of ice flowing into it is lost through basal melting within the first few hundred kilometres after flotation begins (L315). The alternatives name distinct processes: buttressing slows inland ice discharge (AAP L306); marine ice sheet instability is a feedback on retrograde beds (NASEM L383-L385); calving is iceberg loss from the shelf front (AAP L302,L306). Only basal melting is the process explicitly responsible for the Amery statistic. The Russian proper name is standardized as Эймери, consistent with actual same-topic order36 and the AAP identification of the Amery Ice Shelf.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/ice-shelf-sources.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-polar-first10-01a142a3/author/source-next2-10/sources/nsidc-ice-shelf.txt",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/misi-sources.json"
          ],
          "locator": "AAP L314-L315; actual CURRENT36 full card",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/ice-shelf-sources.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-polar-first10-01a142a3/author/source-next2-10/sources/nsidc-ice-shelf.txt",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/misi-sources.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "explanation",
          "literal": "Это базальное таяние. На шельфе Эймери таким образом теряется более половины поступающего льда; таяние истончает шельф снизу и может ослаблять его подпирающее действие.",
          "literalSHA256": "7911d816a017f0f22744019b0a476a9320ba82528f5284ac20948d2124b9b65a",
          "primaryGround": "AAP L315 directly states the Amery statistic and defines basal melting as melting beneath the shelf where it interacts with the ocean. AAP L306 describes the shelf buttressing effect, supporting the explanation that shape/thinning can affect associated glacier flow. The spelling Эймери matches the same-topic actual CURRENT36 card for the Amery Ice Shelf.",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/ice-shelf-sources.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-polar-first10-01a142a3/author/source-next2-10/sources/nsidc-ice-shelf.txt",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/misi-sources.json"
          ],
          "locator": "AAP L306,L315,L328",
          "sourcePathsBeforeTechnicalNormalization": [
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/ice-shelf-sources.json",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-polar-first10-01a142a3/author/source-next2-10/sources/nsidc-ice-shelf.txt",
            "/Users/eaafonasev/.codex/worktrees/question-quality-wave6-01a12b0f/mindbattle/docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/misi-sources.json"
          ]
        },
        {
          "group": "note0",
          "literal": "Базальное таяние идёт снизу при контакте основания шельфа с океаном; часть талой воды дальше на север вновь замерзает у основания как морской лёд.",
          "literalSHA256": "6813aab5124f5c3813211cbeedd73d3c82290a7918c6d6f25aba9aa1636737a8",
          "primaryGround": "AAP defines basal melting as melting beneath the shelf where it interacts with ocean water (L315); it also says some meltwater refreezes to the base as marine ice farther north (L315).",
          "sourcePaths": [
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/ice-shelf-sources.json",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/process-v2-polar-first10-01a142a3/author/source-next2-10/sources/nsidc-ice-shelf.txt",
            "docs/content-audits/question-quality-wave-8/coordinator-01a15a0f/source-polar49/raw/misi-sources.json"
          ],
          "locator": "AAP L315",
